LIB_LOAD("pp",{"pp1":{"challenge":[{"q":"How did Christian discover his burden?","o":["By reading his book","In a dream","From a letter","From a neighbour"],"why":"Reading his book showed him the load he was carrying."},{"q":"What was written on Evangelist's scroll?","o":["\"Flee from the wrath to come\"","\"Go back home\"","\"Wait for help\"","\"Follow the river\""],"why":"The scroll told him to run from the danger ahead."},{"q":"Who said, \"Leave our friends and our nice life behind?\"","o":["Obstinate","Pliable","Help","Evangelist"],"why":"Obstinate couldn't imagine leaving his comforts."},{"q":"What does the name 'Pliable' mean?","o":["Easy to bend","Stubborn","Brave","Wise"],"why":"Pliable bends whichever way he is pushed."},{"q":"Who pulled Christian out of the swamp?","o":["Help","Pliable","Evangelist","Mr Legality"],"why":"Help held out his hand and pulled him out."},{"q":"What do the steps in the swamp stand for?","o":["God's promises","Hard work","Good luck","The road home"],"why":"The steps are God's promises that hold you up when you feel low."},{"q":"What did Pliable end up doing at home?","o":["Gossiping about Christian","Setting out again","Warning the city","Looking for Help"],"why":"Quitters often end up criticising those who keep going."},{"q":"What did Evangelist say about Mr Legality?","o":["He has never freed anyone from their burden","He lives too far away","He charges too much money","He wasn't at home"],"why":"Rules alone can't remove the burden."},{"q":"Why did Christian head towards the tall hill?","o":["He followed Mr Worldly Wiseman's advice","Evangelist sent him there","He wanted to see the view","He was chasing Pliable"],"why":"He took the shortcut, and it almost ruined him."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"No man, having put his hand to the plough, and ___, is fit for the kingdom of God.\"","o":["looking back","standing still","falling asleep","turning aside"],"why":"Luke 9:62. Once you start, don't look back."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Complete Evangelist's words: \"Keep that ___ in your eye.\"","o":["light","gate","book","crown"],"why":"Keep that light in your eye. Start with the light you have."},"choices":[{"title":"The expo offer","q":"Two weeks before your exam, a senior student says he can get you \"expo\", the questions before the exam, for ₦5,000. \"Everybody does it. Why stress yourself?\"","o":[{"t":"Say no, and study with a friend instead.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You stayed on the right road, and you brought a companion."},{"t":"Say no, keep studying, and tell a teacher you trust.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You stayed on the right road and protected others too."},{"t":"Pay. Everybody does it.","f":"That's Mr Worldly Wiseman's shortcut. It looks easy, but it can cancel your whole result."},{"t":"Don't pay, but ask him to share it free.","f":"Still the shortcut. The price isn't the problem; the road is."}]},{"title":"The teammate who quits","q":"Your group is building a model for the science fair. One teammate was the most excited at the start. The first time the model falls apart he says, \"This thing no go work. I'm out.\"","o":[{"t":"Encourage him, show him the next small step, and keep working even if he leaves.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christian, you keep pushing towards the far side of the swamp."},{"t":"Quit too.","f":"Then the swamp wins. Pliable's choice doesn't have to be yours."},{"t":"Shout at him in front of everyone.","f":"Leaders persuade; they don't shame people."},{"t":"Mock him in the class WhatsApp group.","f":"That's what Pliable's neighbours did. Gossip never builds a team."}]},{"title":"Laughed at at home","q":"You decide to wake up early to pray and read before school. Your older cousin laughs: \"Look at this one, {she} wants to become Pastor!\"","o":[{"t":"Keep going quietly, and stay kind to your cousin.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Christian prayed for his family instead of fighting them."},{"t":"Stop, so they leave you alone.","f":"Christian kept going even when his own family laughed."},{"t":"Argue until you win.","f":"Winning the argument isn't the goal. Staying on the road is."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"road","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 in real life."},{"sc":"field","n":"🧭 Choose your advisers. Before you take advice, ask: Who is this person? Does it match God's word? What happens if they're wrong?"},{"sc":"swamp","n":"💪 Finish what you start. Every project, team and business hits a swamp. People who push through become the people others trust."},{"sc":"field","n":"🤝 Be someone's Help. Explaining maths to a classmate, or encouraging a friend who failed a test, is holding out your hand in the swamp."},{"sc":"road","n":"↩️ Turn back fast. A captain who changes a bad plan at half-time. A student who says, \"I was wrong.\" That's what Christian did."}],"stops":{"pp1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"city","n":"Meet Christian. He lives in a busy, noisy town called the {City of Destruction}."},{"sc":"city","n":"One day, he reads a book. The more he reads, the more scared he gets. He starts to shake. He starts to cry."},{"sc":"city","n":"On his back is a huge, heavy {burden}. It is the weight of every wrong thing he has ever done. And it is getting heavier."},{"sc":"city","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"What shall I do?","b":true},{"sc":"home","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"My dear family, this load is crushing me! The book says our city will be destroyed by fire from heaven. We must escape!"},{"sc":"home","n":"His family stares at him. They think he is going crazy. \"Go and sleep,\" they say. \"You'll be fine tomorrow.\""},{"sc":"night","n":"But he can't sleep. Next day they laugh at him. Then they shout at him. Then they ignore him. So he goes to his room and prays for them."},{"sc":"field","n":"One day, alone in a field, he cries out again. He wants to run. But which way?"},{"sc":"field","w":"evangelist","e":"smile","t":"Why are you crying, my son?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"This book says I must face judgment. I'm not ready! And I don't know where to go."},{"sc":"field","w":"evangelist","e":"smile","t":"Then why are you standing still?"},{"sc":"field","n":"Evangelist gives him a {scroll}. It says: \"Flee from the {wrath} to come.\""},{"sc":"field","w":"evangelist","e":"smile","t":"Do you see that little gate far away?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"No, I can't see it."},{"sc":"field","w":"evangelist","e":"smile","t":"Do you see that shining light? Keep that light in your eye. Walk straight to it, and you will find the {Wicket Gate}. Knock there.","b":true},{"sc":"road","n":"So Christian starts to RUN! His family screams, \"Come back!\" But he puts his fingers in his ears and keeps running."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian","e":"big","t":"Life! Life! Eternal life!","b":true}],"quote":{"text":"Keep that light in your eye, and go up directly thereto.","who":"Evangelist"},"lesson":{"title":"Face it, then move","text":"Christian didn't pretend his problem wasn't there. And the moment he got direction, he moved, even while people laughed. You don't need to see the whole road. Start with the light you have."},"think":"Have you ever known something was right, but people around you laughed at it? What helped you keep going?","quiz":[{"q":"What was on Christian's back?","o":["A heavy burden","A school bag","A sword","A water pot"],"why":"A big, heavy burden. It stands for the weight of every wrong thing he had done."},{"q":"What was the name of Christian's hometown?","o":["The City of Destruction","The Celestial City","Vanity Fair","The Village of Morality"],"why":"He lived in the City of Destruction, a town heading for ruin."},{"q":"What did his family think when he told them?","o":["That he was going crazy","That he was right","That he was joking","That he was sick with malaria"],"why":"They thought something had gone wrong in his head, so they told him to go and sleep."},{"q":"Christian couldn't see the gate. What did Evangelist tell him to follow?","o":["The shining light","A river","A road sign","A flying bird"],"why":"\"Keep that light in your eye.\" You don't have to see the whole road to take the first step."},{"q":"What did Christian shout as he ran?","o":["\"Life! Life! Eternal life!\"","\"Help me!\"","\"I'll be back!\"","\"Wait for me!\""],"why":"He ran towards life, and he didn't look back."}]},"pp1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"city","n":"The whole street comes out to watch Christian run. Some laugh. Some threaten. Two neighbours chase after him to drag him back."},{"sc":"city","n":"Their names? {Obstinate} and {Pliable}."},{"sc":"road","w":"obstinate","e":"frown","t":"Oya! Come back home with us!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"I can't. Our city is going to be destroyed. Come with me instead!"},{"sc":"road","w":"obstinate","e":"frown","t":"What?! Leave our friends and our nice life behind? Are you mad?"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"Everything you leave is nothing next to what I'm going to find: a home in heaven that can never be destroyed."},{"sc":"road","w":"obstinate","e":"frown","t":"Rubbish! Forget your book. Are you coming back or not?"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"No, not I. I have {put my hand to the plough}.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"pliable","e":"big","t":"Wait o! If what he says is true, his road is better than ours. I'm going with him!"},{"sc":"road","w":"obstinate","e":"frown","t":"Another fool! Fine. I'm going home."},{"sc":"road","n":"Obstinate stomps back to the city alone. Christian and Pliable walk on together."},{"sc":"field","w":"pliable","e":"big","t":"So tell me, what will we get there?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"A kingdom that never ends. Crowns of glory. Clothes that shine like the sun. And no more crying, ever."},{"sc":"field","w":"pliable","e":"big","t":"Wow! Come on, let's walk faster!"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"I can't go as fast as I want. This load on my back is too heavy."},{"sc":"field","n":"Did you notice? Pliable only asked about the prizes. He never asked about the cost. Hmm..."}],"quote":{"text":"No, not I, because I have put my hand to the plough.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Be committed, not just excited","text":"Obstinate was firm about the wrong thing. Pliable was excited about the right thing, but only for the prizes. Christian stood firm without being rude, and still invited others to come. Leaders persuade; they don't force."},"think":"Do you know someone like Pliable, super excited at the start of everything? Are you ever like Pliable?","quiz":[{"q":"Which two neighbours chased after Christian?","o":["Obstinate and Pliable","Help and Evangelist","Faithful and Hopeful","Simple and Sloth"],"why":"Obstinate and Pliable came to drag him back."},{"q":"What does the name 'Obstinate' mean?","o":["Stubborn","Kind","Fast","Easy to bend"],"why":"Obstinate means stubborn. He would not change his mind."},{"q":"\"I have put my hand to the plough\" means...","o":["I have started and I won't turn back","I want to become a farmer","I am very tired","I want to go home"],"why":"A farmer who looks back while ploughing makes a crooked line. Christian would not look back."},{"q":"Why did Pliable decide to go with Christian?","o":["He liked hearing about the prizes","Obstinate told him to","He was running from debt","He wanted to meet Evangelist"],"why":"Pliable only asked about the prizes, never the cost. That's excitement, not commitment."},{"q":"Why couldn't Christian walk faster?","o":["His heavy load","His slippers cut","He was hungry","Pliable was too slow"],"why":"The burden on his back slowed him down."}]},"pp1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"swamp","n":"Busy talking, not looking... SPLASH! They both fall into a deep, muddy swamp."},{"sc":"swamp","n":"It is called the {Slough of Despond}. The swamp of discouragement."},{"sc":"swamp","n":"Christian's heavy load pulls him down. He starts to sink."},{"sc":"swamp","w":"pliable","e":"shock","t":"Christian! Where are you?! Is THIS the happy journey you promised me?"},{"sc":"swamp","w":"pliable","e":"frown","t":"If it's this bad at the start, what about the rest? You can have your wonderful country. I'm out!"},{"sc":"swamp","n":"Pliable struggles out on the side nearest HOME, and runs away. Christian never sees him again."},{"sc":"swamp","n":"Now Christian is alone. He can't climb out. But he keeps pushing towards the side nearest the GATE."},{"sc":"swamp","n":"Then a man arrives. His name is {Help}."},{"sc":"swamp","w":"help","e":"smile","t":"What are you doing in there? Why didn't you use the {steps}?"},{"sc":"swamp","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"Fear was chasing me so hard, I ran the quickest way and fell in.","b":true},{"sc":"swamp","w":"help","e":"smile","t":"Give me your hand.","b":true},{"sc":"field","n":"Help pulls him out and puts him on solid ground. Christian is free to go on."},{"sc":"field","w":"help","e":"smile","t":"There ARE strong steps through this swamp: God's promises. But when people panic, they miss them."},{"sc":"home","n":"Meanwhile, Pliable gets home. His neighbours laugh at him for quitting. But soon, he joins them... gossiping about Christian."}],"quote":{"text":"Fear followed me so hard, that I fled the next way and fell in.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Keep going through the mud","text":"Every big dream has a swamp. Pliable quit because he only came for the prizes. Christian kept pushing the right way, even when he was stuck. Panic makes you miss the steps. And be a Help: hold out your hand to someone who is stuck."},"think":"Who has been a 'Help' to you? How can you be a Help to someone at school this week?","proverb":{"text":"Onye aghana nwanne ya.","lang":"Igbo","mean":"Do not leave your brother or sister behind."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was the swamp called?","o":["The Slough of Despond","The River of Life","The Valley of Shadows","Hill Difficulty"],"why":"The Slough of Despond: the swamp of discouragement."},{"q":"What does 'despond' mean?","o":["To lose hope","To run fast","To shout loudly","To be very happy"],"why":"Despond means to lose hope. Discouragement is a swamp every pilgrim meets."},{"q":"What did Pliable do in the swamp?","o":["Climbed out on the side nearest home and left","Went to find a rope","Waited on the other side","Called Evangelist"],"why":"He quit at the first difficulty and went back home."},{"q":"Why did Christian miss the steps?","o":["Fear made him rush","It was too dark","Pliable hid them","There were no steps"],"why":"Panic made him run the quickest way. Decisions made in fear are often poor ones."},{"q":"What did Help say to Christian?","o":["\"Give me your hand\"","\"Swim harder\"","\"Go back home\"","\"Wait till morning\""],"why":"Help didn't lecture him. He held out his hand. That's servant leadership."}]},"pp1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"field","n":"Christian walks on alone. Then a well-dressed man comes over. Fine clothes. Big talk. Everybody knows him."},{"sc":"field","n":"He is {Mr Worldly Wiseman}, from the big town of {Carnal Policy}."},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"smirk","t":"My friend! Where are you going with that heavy load?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"To the little gate ahead, sir. They will show me how to get free of my burden."},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"smirk","t":"Will you take my advice?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"If it is good, I will. I need good advice.","b":true},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"smirk","t":"Who told you to go that way?"},{"sc":"field","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"A good man called Evangelist."},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"frown","t":"Bad advice! That road is full of trouble: hunger, lions, dragons, darkness, even death. I'm older than you. Listen to me."},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"smirk","t":"I know a shortcut. In the village of {Morality} lives Mr {Legality}. He takes loads off people's backs, quick-quick!"},{"sc":"field","w":"wiseman","e":"smirk","t":"If he's not around, his son {Civility} can do it. Cheap houses, good food, respectable neighbours. Bring your family!"},{"sc":"field","n":"It sounds so easy. Christian leaves the right road and heads for a tall hill near Mr Legality's house."},{"sc":"hill","n":"But up close, the hill hangs over the road like it will fall on his head. Fire flashes out of it. His load feels heavier than ever."},{"sc":"hill","n":"Christian freezes, sweating and shaking. He wishes he had never listened."},{"sc":"hill","n":"Then he sees Evangelist coming. Christian's face burns with shame."},{"sc":"hill","w":"evangelist","e":"stern","t":"What are you doing here, Christian? Didn't I show you the way? Why did you turn aside so fast?"},{"sc":"hill","n":"Christian tells him everything. He falls down crying, \"Woe is me!\""},{"sc":"hill","w":"evangelist","e":"stern","t":"Mr Worldly Wiseman only cares about this world. Mr Legality has never freed anyone from their burden. It was a trap to pull you off the road."},{"sc":"hill","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"Is there any hope for me? Can I still go to the gate?"},{"sc":"road","w":"evangelist","e":"smile","t":"Yes. The man at the gate will welcome you. Just don't turn aside again."},{"sc":"road","n":"Evangelist smiles. And Christian runs back to the right road, faster than ever."}],"quote":{"text":"If it be good, I will; for I stand in need of good counsel.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Check the advice, own the mistake","text":"Fine clothes and big talk don't make good advice. Warning signs: they insult your guide and promise big results with no cost. When Christian was corrected, he made no excuses. He turned back fast. Great leaders still make mistakes; they just turn around quickly."},"think":"What 'shortcuts' are offered to students, like exam expo or paying for marks? How are they like the road to Mr Legality?","quiz":[{"q":"Which town was Mr Worldly Wiseman from?","o":["Carnal Policy","Morality","The City of Destruction","Vanity Fair"],"why":"Carnal Policy: a town where people live only for comfort and whatever pays."},{"q":"Who did he say could take off Christian's burden?","o":["Mr Legality or his son Civility","Evangelist","Help","Pliable"],"why":"He sent Christian to Mr Legality. But rules and good manners alone can't remove the burden."},{"q":"What happened when Christian got near the hill?","o":["It looked ready to fall on him, and fire flashed out","He climbed it easily","He found Mr Legality at home","He met Pliable again"],"why":"The shortcut looked easy from far away. Up close, it was terrifying."},{"q":"What did Christian do when Evangelist corrected him?","o":["Admitted his mistake and went back","Argued and walked away","Blamed Mr Worldly Wiseman and kept going","Went back home"],"why":"No excuses. He owned it and turned around."},{"q":"Which one is a warning sign of bad advice?","o":["It promises big results with no cost","It comes from someone who cares about you","It matches God's word","It tells you the truth even when it's hard"],"why":"Shortcuts that promise everything for nothing usually cost the most in the end."}]}}},"pp2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Christian do at the Wicket Gate?","o":["Knocked again and again","Climbed over the wall","Waited quietly","Went back home"],"why":"He knocked, and the door was opened."},{"q":"Who was captain of the castle near the gate?","o":["Beelzebub","Goodwill","The Interpreter","Mr Legality"],"why":"Beelzebub's men shoot arrows at people coming to the gate."},{"q":"Goodwill said the narrow way was...","o":["As straight as a ruler","Full of shortcuts","Wide and easy","Hidden in the bush"],"why":"The right road doesn't bend to every shortcut."},{"q":"In the Interpreter's picture, what was written on the man's lips?","o":["Truth","Money","Jokes","Nothing"],"why":"A true guide speaks the truth."},{"q":"What did the sweeping in the dusty room stand for?","o":["The law, which shows sin but can't clean it","The Gospel","Hard work","Good luck"],"why":"Rules show the dirt. Grace washes it away."},{"q":"Passion wanted his good things...","o":["Right now","Next year","When he grew up","Never"],"why":"Passion couldn't wait, and ended in rags."},{"q":"Who secretly kept the fire burning?","o":["A man behind the wall pouring oil","The devil","Christian","Patience"],"why":"Christ keeps God's work alive in the heart."},{"q":"Why did the crowd at the palace door hold back?","o":["They were afraid of the men in armour","They were tired","They had no money","They didn't want to go in"],"why":"Only one man was brave enough to say, \"Set down my name.\""},{"q":"Who said, \"I am what I was not once\"?","o":["The man in the iron cage","Goodwill","Passion","The brave man"],"why":"He was once a strong pilgrim, but he drifted away."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; ___, and it shall be opened unto you.\"","o":["knock","wait","run","shout"],"why":"Matthew 7:7. Doors open for those who knock."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Complete the brave man's words: \"Set down my ___, sir!\"","o":["name","sword","book","crown"],"why":"He was the first to put his name down."},"choices":[{"title":"Knock and ask","q":"You don't understand today's maths topic. You want to ask the teacher, but you're scared your classmates will laugh at you.","o":[{"t":"Ask the teacher after class, or ask in class anyway.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Christian knocked again and again. Doors open for people who knock."},{"t":"Pretend you understand.","f":"Then the gate stays shut. Pretending never opened any door."},{"t":"Copy a friend's homework.","f":"That's a shortcut, and shortcuts lead to Mr Legality's hill."},{"t":"Give up on maths.","f":"Christian didn't give up when no one answered at first. Keep knocking!"}]},{"title":"Now or later?","q":"You got ₦10,000 for your birthday. You've been saving for a school trip. Your friend says, \"Let's spend it all on data and snacks today!\"","o":[{"t":"Keep most of it for the trip, and maybe enjoy a small treat.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Patience, you're waiting for the best thing."},{"t":"Spend it all today. YOLO!","f":"That's Passion. It feels great today, and leaves rags tomorrow."},{"t":"Lend all of it to your friend.","f":"Generous, but your plan matters too. Patience keeps his eyes on the goal."}]},{"title":"Set down my name","q":"Your school needs someone to lead the clean-up club. Everyone wants the club to work, but nobody raises a hand. Some seniors say it's a \"punishment job\".","o":[{"t":"Raise your hand and say, \"Put my name down.\"","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You're the brave man at the palace door."},{"t":"Wait for somebody else to volunteer.","f":"That's the crowd at the door: wanting the prize, but frozen by fear."},{"t":"Laugh at whoever volunteers.","f":"Mockers never build anything. Be the builder."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"road","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 in real life."},{"sc":"gate","n":"🚪 Knock. Ask the teacher, apply for the scholarship, join the club. Doors open for people who knock."},{"sc":"house","n":"🖼️ Pick your guides. Before you follow anyone, online or offline, check them against the picture: truth on their lips, the world behind their back."},{"sc":"house","n":"⏳ Wait for the best. Saving money, finishing school, building a skill: Patience wins in the end."},{"sc":"palace","n":"✍️ Set down your name. When everyone holds back, be the first to volunteer for the hard job."}],"stops":{"pp2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Christian runs back to the right road. He doesn't stop to talk to anybody. Not today!"},{"sc":"gate","n":"At last he reaches the {Wicket Gate}. Above it are the words: \"Knock, and it shall be opened unto you.\""},{"sc":"gate","n":"So he knocks. Once. Twice. Again and again."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"May I come in? I've messed up before... but will you still open for me?"},{"sc":"gate","n":"At last a serious-looking man comes to the gate. His name is {Goodwill}."},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"stern","t":"Who is there? Where do you come from? What do you want?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"I'm a poor man with a heavy burden. I come from the City of Destruction, and I'm going to Mount Zion. Please, will you let me in?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"big","t":"I am willing with all my heart!","b":true},{"sc":"gate","n":"As Christian steps in, Goodwill PULLS him through, fast. \"Why did you do that?\" Christian asks."},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"stern","t":"Close to this gate is a strong castle. Its captain is {Beelzebub}. His men shoot arrows at anyone coming here, to stop them before they get in."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"shock","t":"I rejoice and tremble!","b":true},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"smile","t":"But why did you come alone?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"My neighbours didn't see the danger like I did. Pliable started with me, but he quit at the swamp."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"And honestly, I'm no better. I left the road too, because I listened to Mr Worldly Wiseman."},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"smile","t":"We don't turn anyone away, no matter what they did before. Now look ahead. See that {narrow way}? That's your road. It's as straight as a ruler."},{"sc":"gate","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"Can you take this burden off my back?"},{"sc":"gate","w":"goodwill","e":"smile","t":"Carry it a little longer. When you reach the place of deliverance, it will fall off by itself."},{"sc":"road","n":"Goodwill points to a house further on. \"That is the house of the {Interpreter}. Knock there. He will show you amazing things.\""}],"quote":{"text":"I am willing with all my heart.","who":"Goodwill"},"lesson":{"title":"Knock, and tell the truth","text":"Christian didn't stand outside wishing. He knocked, again and again. And when Goodwill asked questions, he told the truth, even about his own mistake. Leaders ask for help, and they're honest about their failures."},"think":"Is there a 'gate' you're scared to knock on? A teacher to ask, a club to join, or an apology to make?","quiz":[{"q":"What was written above the gate?","o":["\"Knock, and it shall be opened unto you\"","\"No entry\"","\"Pay at the gate\"","\"Come back tomorrow\""],"why":"The gate invited him to knock, and he did, again and again."},{"q":"Who opened the gate?","o":["Goodwill","Evangelist","Help","Obstinate"],"why":"Goodwill opened it, and said he was willing with all his heart."},{"q":"Why did Goodwill pull Christian in so fast?","o":["Beelzebub's men shoot arrows near the gate","It was about to rain","The gate was closing","He was late for dinner"],"why":"The enemy tries hardest to stop people right at the start."},{"q":"What did Christian honestly admit to Goodwill?","o":["He had left the road because of Mr Worldly Wiseman","He had lost his scroll","He wanted to go home","He was scared of the dark"],"why":"He didn't hide his mistake. Honest leaders own their failures."},{"q":"When would Christian's burden fall off?","o":["At the place of deliverance","At the gate","At the Interpreter's house","Never"],"why":"Goodwill told him to carry it a little longer. It would fall off by itself at the right place."}]},"pp2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"house","n":"Christian knocks at the {Interpreter}'s door, again and again. Finally the master of the house comes out."},{"sc":"house","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"Sir, I'm travelling from the City of Destruction to Mount Zion. I was told you would show me things to help me on my journey."},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"Come in. I will show you something that will help you.","b":true},{"sc":"house","n":"He lights a candle and leads Christian into a private room. On the wall hangs a picture of a very serious man."},{"sc":"house","n":"His eyes look up to heaven. The best of books is in his hand. Truth is written on his lips. The world is behind his back. And a gold crown hangs over his head."},{"sc":"house","w":"christian","e":"shock","t":"What does this mean?"},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"This man is the kind of guide the Lord has chosen to lead you through hard places. Remember him."},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"stern","t":"Many people will pretend to lead you right. But their road goes down to death."},{"sc":"dusty","n":"Next, he takes Christian into a big {parlour} full of dust. It has NEVER been swept."},{"sc":"dusty","n":"A man starts sweeping. The dust flies everywhere! Christian almost chokes."},{"sc":"dusty","n":"Then the Interpreter calls a girl. \"Bring water and sprinkle the room.\" She does, and now the room is swept clean, easily."},{"sc":"dusty","w":"christian","e":"shock","t":"What does this mean?"},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"The room is a heart that has never been changed. The dust is sin. The sweeping is the law: it only stirs the dust up."},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"The water is the Gospel. Rules can show you the dirt, but only God's grace can wash it away."}],"quote":{"text":"Come in; I will show thee that which will be profitable to thee.","who":"Interpreter"},"lesson":{"title":"Choose your guides carefully","text":"The picture shows what a true guide looks like: eyes on God, the Bible in hand, truth on their lips, and not chasing the world. Check people against that picture before you follow them, online or offline. And real change starts inside, not just with keeping rules."},"think":"Who are the guides you follow, on social media, at school or at church? Do they match the picture?","quiz":[{"q":"Whose house did Christian visit after the gate?","o":["The Interpreter's","Mr Legality's","Pliable's","Beelzebub's"],"why":"Goodwill sent him to the Interpreter, who explains hidden meanings."},{"q":"In the picture, where was the world?","o":["Behind the man's back","In his hands","On his head","In his pocket"],"why":"A true guide has put the world behind him. He isn't chasing money and fame."},{"q":"Why did the Interpreter show Christian the picture?","o":["To show him the kind of guide to follow","To sell it to him","To decorate the room","To scare him"],"why":"So that Christian could tell true guides from fake ones."},{"q":"What happened when the man swept the dusty room?","o":["Dust flew everywhere and Christian almost choked","The room became clean at once","Nothing happened","The broom broke"],"why":"Sweeping is like the law. It shows the dirt but can't clean it."},{"q":"What did the water stand for?","o":["The Gospel, God's grace","Rain","Hard work","More rules"],"why":"Only grace makes the heart truly clean."}]},"pp2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"house","n":"In the next room, two little boys sit on two chairs. Their names are {Passion} and {Patience}."},{"sc":"house","n":"Passion is upset and restless. Patience is calm and quiet."},{"sc":"house","w":"christian","e":"smile","t":"Why is Passion so unhappy?"},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"Their guardian wants them to wait until next year for their best things. Passion wants everything NOW. Patience is willing to wait."},{"sc":"house","n":"Then someone brings Passion a big bag of treasure and pours it at his feet."},{"sc":"house","w":"passion","e":"big","t":"Yes! It's all mine! Ha ha, Patience, you're still waiting!"},{"sc":"house","w":"patience","e":"smile","t":"It's okay. I can wait."},{"sc":"house","n":"But watch. In a short time, Passion has wasted everything. Nothing is left but rags."},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"Passion is like people who must have everything in this world, right now. Patience is like people who wait for the world to come."},{"sc":"house","w":"christian","e":"big","t":"Now I see that Patience has the best wisdom! He waits for the best things, and his will last when Passion has only rags.","b":true},{"sc":"house","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"Yes. The things we see don't last long. The things we can't see last forever."},{"sc":"fire","n":"Next, Christian sees a fire burning against a wall. Someone keeps throwing water on it to put it out... but the fire burns HIGHER and hotter!"},{"sc":"fire","n":"So the Interpreter takes him round to the other side of the wall. There, a man is secretly pouring oil into the fire."},{"sc":"fire","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"The fire is God's work in a person's heart. The one throwing water is the devil."},{"sc":"fire","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"The man with the oil is Christ. He keeps the fire burning with His grace, even when you can't see how."}],"quote":{"text":"Now I see that Patience has the best wisdom.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Wait for the best","text":"Passion grabbed everything now and ended in rags. Patience waited and won. Leaders can say 'not yet' to something good today, for something better tomorrow. And when people try to put out your fire, remember who keeps pouring the oil."},"think":"What is one thing you want RIGHT NOW that would be even better if you waited for it?","proverb":{"text":"Sannu sannu bata hana zuwa.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Going slowly does not stop you from arriving."},"quiz":[{"q":"What were the two boys called?","o":["Passion and Patience","Obstinate and Pliable","Simple and Sloth","Faithful and Hopeful"],"why":"Passion and Patience: one wanted it now, one was willing to wait."},{"q":"What did Passion want?","o":["Everything, right now","To wait for next year","To go to school","To give his things away"],"why":"Passion couldn't wait for anything."},{"q":"What happened to Passion's treasure?","o":["He wasted it all and was left with rags","He saved it","He shared it with Patience","He hid it"],"why":"Grabbing everything now often ends with nothing."},{"q":"Why did the fire keep burning higher?","o":["A man behind the wall kept pouring oil into it","It was raining fire","Nobody poured water on it","Christian fanned it"],"why":"Someone you couldn't see was keeping it alive."},{"q":"Who does the man with the oil stand for?","o":["Christ, keeping God's work alive in the heart","The Interpreter","Christian","The devil"],"why":"Christ keeps the fire burning with His grace, even when we can't see how."}]},"pp2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"palace","n":"The Interpreter leads Christian to a beautiful palace. People dressed in gold are walking on its roof."},{"sc":"palace","n":"A big crowd stands at the door. They want to go in, but they're too scared. Men in armour guard the door, ready to hurt anyone who tries."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Nearby, a man sits at a table with a book and ink, ready to write the name of anyone who will go in. Nobody moves."},{"sc":"palace","n":"Then one man with a brave face walks up to the table."},{"sc":"palace","w":"brave","e":"stern","t":"Set down my name, sir!","b":true},{"sc":"palace","n":"He puts on a helmet, draws his sword, and charges at the guards! They fight hard. He gets wounded, but he doesn't stop. He cuts his way through, right into the palace!"},{"sc":"palace","n":"Voices sing from the roof: \"Come in, come in; eternal glory thou shalt win.\""},{"sc":"palace","w":"christian","e":"big","t":"I think I know what this means!"},{"sc":"cage","n":"Then the Interpreter takes him into a very dark room. A man sits inside an {iron cage}, looking at the floor and sighing as if his heart will break."},{"sc":"cage","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"Who are you?"},{"sc":"cage","w":"caged","e":"worried","t":"I am what I was not once.","b":true},{"sc":"cage","w":"caged","e":"worried","t":"I was once a strong pilgrim. Everybody thought I was doing well. But I stopped watching. Little by little, I let wrong things take over my life."},{"sc":"cage","w":"interpreter","e":"stern","t":"Remember this man, Christian. Let him be a warning to you."},{"sc":"cage","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"This is fearful! God help me to watch and pray, so I never end up like him."},{"sc":"night","n":"One more room. A man is getting out of bed, shaking. He dreamed that Judgment Day had come, and he wasn't ready."},{"sc":"road","w":"interpreter","e":"smile","t":"Keep all these things in your mind, Christian. Let them push you forward on your way."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian","e":"big","t":"Here I have seen things rare and useful. Thank you, good Interpreter!"}],"quote":{"text":"Set down my name, sir.","who":"Brave"},"lesson":{"title":"Step forward, and keep watching","text":"Everyone wanted the prize, but fear froze them. One man said, \"Set down my name,\" and fought his way in. Leaders step forward first. But the man in the cage shows that even strong people can drift. Stay watchful, and don't let small bad habits pull you away."},"think":"Where is everyone standing at the door, too scared to go in? Could you be the first to say, \"Set down my name\"?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the brave man say to the man with the book?","o":["\"Set down my name, sir!\"","\"I'm too scared\"","\"Let me go home\"","\"Open the gate\""],"why":"He volunteered first, while everyone else held back."},{"q":"Why did the crowd stay outside the palace?","o":["They were afraid of the men in armour","The door was locked","It was night time","They weren't invited"],"why":"Fear stopped them, not a locked door."},{"q":"What did the people on the roof sing?","o":["\"Come in, come in; eternal glory thou shalt win\"","\"Go away, go away\"","\"Happy birthday to you\"","\"Wait for tomorrow\""],"why":"Those who push through fear are welcomed in."},{"q":"How did the man end up in the iron cage?","o":["He stopped watching and let wrong things take over, little by little","He was arrested","He got lost","Someone pushed him in"],"why":"Drifting happens slowly. That's why leaders stay watchful."},{"q":"What did the Interpreter want Christian to do with everything he saw?","o":["Keep it in his mind to push him forward","Forget it quickly","Tell Obstinate about it","Write a song"],"why":"The lessons were meant to keep him moving forward on the road."}]}}},"pp3":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where did Christian's burden fall off?","o":["At the Cross","At the Wicket Gate","In the Slough of Despond","At Palace Beautiful"],"why":"At the Cross, all by itself."},{"q":"What did Christian say when his burden fell off?","o":["\"He hath given me rest by His sorrow, and life by His death\"","\"What shall I do?\"","\"Set down my name\"","\"I see no danger\""],"why":"He knew who had set him free."},{"q":"What did the Shining Ones do with Christian's rags?","o":["Took them away and gave him new clothes","Washed them","Burned them in front of him","Left them on"],"why":"Forgiven people get new clothes!"},{"q":"Who said, \"I see no danger\"?","o":["Simple","Sloth","Presumption","Hypocrisy"],"why":"Simple couldn't see the danger he was in."},{"q":"Formalist and Hypocrisy came from the land of...","o":["Vain-glory","Destruction","Morality","Beulah"],"why":"Vain-glory: the land of showing off for praise."},{"q":"Christian sang: \"Better, though difficult, the ___ way to go.\"","o":["right","easy","short","fast"],"why":"Hard-right beats easy-wrong."},{"q":"Where did Christian lose his roll?","o":["In the arbour where he slept","In the swamp","At the Cross","On the road"],"why":"Too much comfort cost him his roll."},{"q":"What did Timorous and Mistrust warn Christian about?","o":["Lions on the road","A flood","Thieves","A giant"],"why":"They saw lions and ran. Christian went forward."},{"q":"What was the Porter's name?","o":["Watchful","Goodwill","Help","Evangelist"],"why":"Watchful the Porter guarded Palace Beautiful."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Put on the whole ___ of God.\"","o":["armour","coat","crown","shoes"],"why":"Ephesians 6:11. Get equipped before the battle."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Christian's first name was...","o":["Graceless","Careless","Fearless","Helpless"],"why":"\"My name is now Christian, but my name at the first was Graceless.\""},"choices":[{"title":"Wake them up","q":"It's three months to WAEC. Your friends say, \"We still get time. We'll start reading next month.\" Every evening they watch films instead.","o":[{"t":"Warn them kindly, and invite them to read with you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christian, you care enough to wake people up, even if they don't thank you."},{"t":"Join them. You still get time.","f":"That's Sloth: \"Yet a little more sleep.\" Time runs out faster than you think."},{"t":"Say nothing. Every tub must stand on its own bottom.","f":"That's Presumption talking. Leaders care about the people around them."},{"t":"Laugh at them and post about it.","f":"Mocking never woke anybody up. Kindness does."}]},{"title":"Climb or go round?","q":"Your house is training for inter-house sports. Training is at 6am and it's tough. Some teammates plan to fake injuries to skip training, but still run on sports day.","o":[{"t":"Keep training, even when it's slow and painful, and encourage the others.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"Better, though difficult, the right way to go.\""},{"t":"Fake an injury too.","f":"That's the road called Danger. Faking catches up with you."},{"t":"Quit the team.","f":"Christian didn't quit when the hill got steep. He crawled if he had to."}]},{"title":"The lost roll","q":"You've been on your phone until 2am every night. Today you realise you forgot to submit an important assignment. It was due yesterday.","o":[{"t":"Tell your teacher the truth, ask to submit it, and change your phone habit.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Christian went back for his roll. Leaders fix mistakes instead of hiding them."},{"t":"Make up an excuse.","f":"That just adds a second mistake to the first."},{"t":"Blame your phone and do nothing.","f":"The arbour wasn't to blame. Christian owned it, went back and fixed it."},{"t":"Give up on that subject.","f":"Christian lost his roll, but he didn't lose the journey. Go back and find it!"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"road","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 in real life."},{"sc":"cross","n":"🎈 Drop the guilt. When you mess up, own it, ask forgiveness, and move on lighter. You lead better without the load."},{"sc":"road","n":"⏰ Wake people up kindly. Real friends warn you, even when you don't want to hear it."},{"sc":"climb","n":"⛰️ Choose the hard right road. Studying, training, telling the truth: \"Better, though difficult, the right way to go.\""},{"sc":"arbour","n":"🐜 Be like the ant. Do your work without anybody standing over you."},{"sc":"lions","n":"🦁 Walk in the middle of the path. Many 'lions' are on chains. Listen to wise people, and keep going."}],"stops":{"pp3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Christian runs up a road with a wall on each side. The wall is called {Salvation}. His load is still heavy, but he keeps running."},{"sc":"cross","n":"He comes to a little hill. On top of it stands a Cross. A little lower down is an open tomb."},{"sc":"cross","w":"christian","e":"worried","t":"This load... I can hardly climb any more."},{"sc":"cross","n":"Just as Christian reaches the Cross... the straps snap. His burden comes loose from his shoulders!"},{"sc":"crossroll","n":"It falls off his back and starts rolling. Rolling, rolling, rolling... down the hill and into the mouth of the tomb. Gone! He never sees it again."},{"sc":"cross","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"He hath given me rest by His sorrow, and life by His death!","b":true},{"sc":"cross","n":"Christian stands still, staring. How can just looking at the Cross take his load away? He looks, and looks, until tears run down his face."},{"sc":"cross","n":"Then three {Shining Ones} come to him. \"Peace be to you,\" they say."},{"sc":"cross","w":"shining","e":"smile","t":"Your sins are forgiven."},{"sc":"cross","n":"The second Shining One takes away his dirty rags and dresses him in brand-new clothes."},{"sc":"cross","w":"shining","e":"smile","t":"Here is a mark on your forehead, and a sealed {roll}. Read it as you run, and hand it in at the gate of the Celestial City."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"I came here carrying my sin, and nothing could ease my pain. What a place is this! Blessed Cross! Blessed be the Man who was put to shame for me!"},{"sc":"road","n":"Christian jumps for joy. One, two, THREE times! Then he goes on his way, singing at the top of his voice."}],"quote":{"text":"He hath given me rest by His sorrow, and life by His death.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Lead from freedom","text":"Christian tried running, Mr Legality and his own effort. Nothing removed the load. It fell off at the Cross. Leaders who know they're forgiven don't have to fake being perfect. They can admit mistakes, forgive others, and lead with joy."},"think":"Is there a mistake or guilty feeling you keep carrying around? Who is a safe person you could talk to about it?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the wall on both sides of the road called?","o":["Salvation","Destruction","Difficulty","Patience"],"why":"The road to the Cross was walled by Salvation."},{"q":"Where did Christian's burden fall off?","o":["At the Cross","At the Wicket Gate","In the swamp","At the Interpreter's house"],"why":"Nothing else could remove it. It fell off at the Cross, by itself, just as Goodwill said."},{"q":"Where did the burden roll to?","o":["Into an open tomb","Into a river","Back to his house","Up the hill"],"why":"It rolled into the tomb, and he never saw it again."},{"q":"What did the three Shining Ones give him?","o":["Forgiveness, new clothes, a mark and a sealed roll","A sword and a shield","A bag of money","A horse to ride"],"why":"Forgiven, newly dressed, marked and given a roll: Christian was a new man."},{"q":"What did Christian do after his burden fell off?","o":["Jumped for joy three times and sang","Went back home","Fell asleep","Tried to pick it up again"],"why":"Freedom makes you want to dance!"}]},"pp3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"At the bottom of the hill, a little off the road, three men lie fast asleep. Iron chains are locked round their ankles."},{"sc":"road","n":"Their names are {Simple}, {Sloth} and {Presumption}."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"shock","t":"Wake up! You're like people sleeping on top of a ship's mast with the deep sea under you! Come, I'll help you take off your chains!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"If the roaring lion comes by, you'll be his food!"},{"sc":"road","w":"simple","e":"sleep","t":"I see no danger.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"sloth","e":"sleep","t":"Yet a little more sleep.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"presumption","e":"sleep","t":"{Every tub must stand upon its own bottom}.","b":true},{"sc":"road","n":"And they go straight back to sleep. Christian walks on, sad that they didn't care about his kindness."},{"sc":"road","n":"Suddenly, two men come tumbling over the wall on the left! Their names are {Formalist} and {Hypocrisy}."},{"sc":"road","w":"formalist","e":"smirk","t":"We were born in the land of {Vain-glory}. We're going to Mount Zion, for praise."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"Why didn't you come in through the gate at the start of the road? The Book says whoever climbs in some other way is a thief and a robber."},{"sc":"road","w":"hypocrisy","e":"smirk","t":"The gate is too far. Everybody in our country takes the shortcut over the wall. We've done it for a thousand years!"},{"sc":"road","w":"formalist","e":"smirk","t":"Anyway, we're in, aren't we? You came through the gate, we came over the wall. What's the difference?"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"I walk by the rule of my Master. You walk by your own ideas.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"hypocrisy","e":"smirk","t":"The only difference is that coat, which your neighbours gave you to hide your shame! Ha!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"smile","t":"This coat was given to me by the Lord of the place I'm going. I also have a mark on my forehead and a sealed roll. You don't have these, because you didn't come through the gate."},{"sc":"road","n":"Formalist and Hypocrisy just look at each other and laugh. Christian walks ahead, reading his roll."}],"quote":{"text":"I walk by the rule of my Master; you walk by the rude working of your fancies.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Care enough to warn, refuse to fake it","text":"Christian tried to wake the sleepers, even though they didn't thank him. Leaders care enough to warn people. And Formalist and Hypocrisy show that HOW you get in matters. Climbing over the wall might look the same from outside, but it isn't the same."},"think":"Have you seen someone get a position or a result the 'over the wall' way? What happened in the end?","quiz":[{"q":"What were the three sleepers called?","o":["Simple, Sloth and Presumption","Faith, Hope and Charity","Obstinate, Pliable and Help","Passion, Patience and Goodwill"],"why":"Simple, Sloth and Presumption, asleep in chains."},{"q":"What did Sloth say?","o":["\"Yet a little more sleep\"","\"I see no danger\"","\"Let's go!\"","\"Help me up\""],"why":"Sloth always wants just a little more sleep."},{"q":"Presumption said, \"Every tub must stand upon its own bottom.\" What did he mean?","o":["Mind your own business, I can take care of myself","I need a bucket","Please help me","Let's go together"],"why":"Presumption was too sure of himself to listen."},{"q":"How did Formalist and Hypocrisy get onto the road?","o":["They climbed over the wall","Through the Wicket Gate","Help carried them","They flew"],"why":"They took the shortcut, skipping the gate."},{"q":"What did Christian have that they didn't?","o":["A new coat, a mark and a sealed roll from the Lord","More money","A horse","Better shoes"],"why":"They came in their own way, so they didn't receive what the Lord gives."}]},"pp3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"climb","n":"Christian comes to the foot of a very steep hill called {Hill Difficulty}. At the bottom is a spring of cool water. He drinks and feels fresh again."},{"sc":"climb","n":"There are two other roads here. One goes left, one goes right, both around the hill. But the narrow way goes straight UP."},{"sc":"climb","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"Better, though difficult, the right way to go, than wrong, though easy, where the end is woe!","b":true},{"sc":"climb","n":"Formalist and Hypocrisy arrive. They look at the steep hill... and take the easy roads instead. The roads are called Danger and Destruction."},{"sc":"climb","n":"One gets lost in a great dark forest. The other stumbles among dark mountains, falls, and never gets up again."},{"sc":"climb","n":"Christian climbs. First running, then walking, then crawling on his hands and knees. It is THAT steep!"},{"sc":"arbour","n":"Halfway up is a pleasant {arbour}, a shady resting place built by the Lord of the hill for tired travellers."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"Christian sits down to rest. He reads his roll and admires his new coat. Then he gets sleepy... and falls fast asleep."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"While he sleeps, the roll slips out of his hand. He doesn't notice."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"Hours later, someone wakes him: \"Go to the ant, thou {sluggard}; consider her ways, and be wise!\""},{"sc":"climb","n":"Christian jumps up and hurries to the top of the hill. It's getting late."},{"sc":"climb","n":"At the top, two men come running towards him, the wrong way! Their names are {Timorous} and {Mistrust}."},{"sc":"climb","w":"timorous","e":"shock","t":"Go back! We're going back! The further we go, the more danger we meet!"},{"sc":"climb","w":"mistrust","e":"shock","t":"There are two lions on the road ahead! Asleep or awake, we don't know. They'll tear us to pieces!"},{"sc":"climb","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"You're making me afraid. But where can I go to be safe? Back home is fire and destruction."},{"sc":"climb","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"To go back is nothing but death. To go forward is fear of death, and life everlasting beyond it. I will yet go forward!","b":true},{"sc":"climb","n":"Timorous and Mistrust run down the hill. Christian reaches into his coat for his roll, to read it for comfort..."},{"sc":"climb","w":"christian2","e":"shock","t":"My roll! Where is my roll?!"}],"quote":{"text":"Better, though difficult, the right way to go, than wrong, though easy, where the end is woe.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Hard-right beats easy-wrong","text":"Formalist and Hypocrisy took the easy roads and were lost. Christian crawled on his knees, but he made it up. Then he rested too long in the comfortable place and lost his roll. Rest is good. Laziness is costly."},"think":"What is your 'Hill Difficulty' right now? What would it look like to keep climbing, even slowly?","proverb":{"text":"Iṣẹ́ ni òògùn ìṣẹ́.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Hard work is the cure for poverty."},"quiz":[{"q":"What did Christian find at the bottom of Hill Difficulty?","o":["A spring of cool water","A lion","A sleeping man","A horse"],"why":"God gave him refreshment before the hard climb."},{"q":"What were the two easy roads around the hill called?","o":["Danger and Destruction","Peace and Joy","Left and Right","Morality and Legality"],"why":"The easy roads had honest names: Danger and Destruction."},{"q":"How did Christian climb the steepest part?","o":["On his hands and knees","In a car","Someone carried him","He gave up"],"why":"He kept going, even when all he could do was crawl."},{"q":"What happened in the arbour?","o":["He fell asleep and dropped his roll","He met Evangelist","He found a lion","He lost his coat"],"why":"A short rest became a long sleep, and he lost something precious."},{"q":"Why did Timorous and Mistrust run back?","o":["They were scared of the lions ahead","It started raining","They were hungry","They lost their way"],"why":"Fear turned them back. Christian chose to go forward."}]},"pp3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"climb","n":"Christian is heartbroken. That roll was his comfort AND his pass into the Celestial City!"},{"sc":"climb","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"Why did I sleep in the daytime? How many steps have I taken for nothing!"},{"sc":"arbour","n":"He kneels down and asks God to forgive him. Then he walks all the way back to the arbour, looking left and right."},{"sc":"arbour","n":"He sits down and cries. Then he looks under the bench... and there it is! His roll!"},{"sc":"arbour","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"Thank God! Thank God!"},{"sc":"lions","n":"He hugs it close and runs back up the hill. But the sun has gone down. It's dark. And he remembers the lions..."},{"sc":"lions","n":"Ahead he sees a beautiful house called {Palace Beautiful}. But on the narrow path in front of it: two lions! He freezes. Should he turn back?"},{"sc":"lions","w":"watchful","e":"stern","t":"Is thy strength so small? Fear not the lions, for they are chained!","b":true},{"sc":"lions","w":"watchful","e":"smile","t":"They are there to test your faith. Keep to the middle of the path, and no harm will come to you."},{"sc":"lions","n":"Christian walks forward, trembling. The lions ROAR! But the chains hold. They can't reach him! He claps his hands and runs to the door."},{"sc":"lions","w":"watchful","e":"smile","t":"What is your name, traveller?"},{"sc":"lions","w":"christian2","e":"smile","t":"My name is now Christian, but my name at the first was {Graceless}.","b":true},{"sc":"lions","n":"The Porter rings a bell. Out come four wise young women: {Discretion}, {Prudence}, {Piety} and {Charity}."},{"sc":"lions","w":"discretion","e":"smile","t":"Come in, blessed one! The Lord of the hill built this house for pilgrims like you."},{"sc":"house","n":"They eat supper together and talk about the Lord of the hill: how He fought the enemy, and gave His life out of love for people. That night Christian sleeps in a room called Peace."},{"sc":"armoury","n":"In the morning they show him the {armoury}: swords, shields, helmets, and shoes that never wear out. Enough for as many pilgrims as there are stars!"},{"sc":"armoury","n":"They also show him Moses' rod, Gideon's trumpets, and the sling and stone that David used to bring down Goliath."},{"sc":"view","n":"From the rooftop, they show him the {Delectable Mountains} far away: woods, vineyards, fruits and springs. From there you can see the gate of the Celestial City!"},{"sc":"armoury","n":"Before he leaves, they dress him from head to toe in armour, ready for any attack on the road."},{"sc":"road","w":"watchful","e":"smile","t":"A pilgrim called Faithful passed by here. He is ahead of you."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian3","e":"big","t":"Faithful! He's my neighbour from home! I must catch up with him!"},{"sc":"road","n":"His four friends walk him down the hill and give him bread, a drink and raisins for the journey. Next: the Valley of Humiliation..."}],"quote":{"text":"Fear not the lions, for they are chained.","who":"Watchful"},"lesson":{"title":"Own it, go back, gear up","text":"Christian didn't blame anyone for the lost roll. He owned it, went back and found it. Then he faced the lions because a wise porter told him the truth: they were chained. Leaders fix mistakes fast, listen to wise voices, and get equipped before the battle."},"think":"What is a 'lion' that scares you: exams, speaking in front of people, a hard conversation? Could it be on a chain?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Christian do when he found his roll was missing?","o":["Asked God to forgive him and went back to find it","Gave up the journey","Blamed the arbour","Asked Timorous for help"],"why":"He owned his mistake and went back to fix it."},{"q":"Where did he find the roll?","o":["Under the bench in the arbour","In the swamp","At the Cross","In his pocket"],"why":"It was right where he had fallen asleep."},{"q":"Why couldn't the lions hurt Christian?","o":["They were chained","They were asleep","Christian killed them","They ran away"],"why":"Many scary things are on chains. The Porter helped him see it."},{"q":"What was Christian's name at first?","o":["Graceless","Pliable","Faithful","Hopeful"],"why":"Graceless became Christian. Grace changes your name!"},{"q":"What did his friends at Palace Beautiful give him before he left?","o":["A full set of armour","A horse","A map","A crown"],"why":"They equipped him for the battles ahead."}]}}},"pp4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What does the name 'Apollyon' mean?","o":["Destroyer","Helper","Friend","King"],"why":"Apollyon means Destroyer."},{"q":"Why did Christian stand his ground instead of running?","o":["His armour didn't cover his back","He was too tired","He wanted to talk","He was lost"],"why":"Turning his back would have made him an easy target."},{"q":"What did Christian say he liked better than Apollyon's kingdom?","o":["The Prince's service, wages, servants, government, company and country","Apollyon's food","The City of Destruction","Nothing at all"],"why":"He knew exactly whose side he was on."},{"q":"What did Christian say about his mistakes?","o":["All true, but the Prince he serves is merciful and ready to forgive","They were all lies","They were Pliable's fault","He would never make mistakes again"],"why":"Honest about the past, confident in mercy."},{"q":"Where was Christian wounded in the battle?","o":["Head, hand and foot","Only his back","He wasn't wounded","Only his ear"],"why":"He was hurt, but he kept fighting."},{"q":"\"We are more than ___ through Him that loved us.\"","o":["conquerors","winners","kings","friends"],"why":"Christian won through the One who loved him."},{"q":"Why did Christian put away his sword in the dark valley?","o":["It was useless against the burning pit","It broke","He gave it away","Apollyon took it"],"why":"He switched to All-Prayer."},{"q":"What did Christian shout to make the fiends back away?","o":["\"I will walk in the strength of the Lord God!\"","\"Go away!\"","\"Help!\"","\"I'm not afraid of you\""],"why":"Not his own strength, but the Lord's."},{"q":"What did the voice ahead of Christian help him realise?","o":["He wasn't alone, and God was with him too","He was going the wrong way","He should go home","He was nearly at the Celestial City"],"why":"Someone else was walking the same dark valley."},{"q":"Complete Psalm 23:4: \"I will fear no ___: for thou art with me.\"","o":["evil","man","night","lion"],"why":"I will fear no evil, for Thou art with me."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Who do you think was the man walking ahead of Christian in the valley?","o":["Faithful, his neighbour","Pliable","Obstinate","Mr Worldly Wiseman"],"why":"Remember? The Porter said Faithful was ahead. You'll meet him in Chapter 5!"},"choices":[{"title":"Your past thrown at you","q":"You're running for class prefect. A rival posts in the class WhatsApp group about mistakes you made last year: a failed test and a punishment you got.","o":[{"t":"Admit it honestly, share what you learned, and keep going.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christian: \"All this is true... but I've been forgiven, and I've changed.\""},{"t":"Deny it and call him a liar.","f":"Christian didn't deny the truth. Honesty takes away the enemy's weapon."},{"t":"Post his mistakes back.","f":"Fighting dirty makes you look like Apollyon, not Christian."},{"t":"Drop out of the election.","f":"Your past doesn't disqualify you. Stand your ground!"}]},{"title":"Knocked down","q":"You prepared for weeks for the inter-school debate final, but your team lost. Everyone is watching to see how you react.","o":[{"t":"Congratulate the winners, then work out what to improve for next time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! \"When I fall, I shall arise.\" Get up, learn, go again."},{"t":"Say you'll never debate again.","f":"Christian's sword flew out of his hand, but he reached for it again."},{"t":"Blame the judges.","f":"Blaming keeps you on the ground. Learning gets you up."},{"t":"Pretend you don't care.","f":"It's okay to feel sad. Then rise."}]},{"title":"Dark thoughts","q":"For a few weeks, thoughts keep coming into your head like \"You're useless\" and \"Nobody cares about you.\"","o":[{"t":"Tell a trusted adult (a parent, teacher, counsellor or pastor) and pray about it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Those thoughts are lies, just like the whispers in the valley. You're not alone, and talking helps morning come."},{"t":"Keep it all to yourself.","f":"Christian felt alone, but he wasn't. Let someone walk with you."},{"t":"Believe the thoughts.","f":"Not every thought in your head is true. You are loved and valued."},{"t":"Scroll on your phone all night to forget.","f":"That keeps you in the dark longer. Reach out instead."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"dawn","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 4 in real life."},{"sc":"valley","n":"🛡️ Know who you serve. When pressure comes, it's much easier to say no if you've already decided whose side you're on."},{"sc":"battle","n":"🧗 Get up again. Every great leader has been knocked down. \"When I fall, I shall arise.\""},{"sc":"shadow","n":"🙏 Change your weapon. Some battles aren't won by arguing harder. Pray, ask for help, try a new approach."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"🧠 Guard your mind. Not every thought in your head is true. Talk to someone you trust when dark thoughts come."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"🌅 Morning comes. Dark seasons end. Keep walking."}],"stops":{"pp4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"valley","n":"Christian walks down into the {Valley of Humiliation}. He hasn't gone far when he sees something coming across the field. Something BIG."},{"sc":"valley","n":"It's a monster called {Apollyon}. Scales like a fish. Wings like a dragon. Feet like a bear. A mouth like a lion. Fire and smoke pour out of his belly."},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian3","e":"shock","t":"Should I run? No. My armour doesn't cover my back. If I turn round, his darts will hit me. I'll stand my ground!"},{"sc":"valley","w":"apollyon","e":"frown","t":"Where have you come from? And where are you going?"},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian3","e":"stern","t":"I've come from the City of Destruction, the place of all evil. I'm going to the City of Zion."},{"sc":"valley","w":"apollyon","e":"frown","t":"Then you are one of MY subjects! That whole country belongs to me. I am its prince and its god. How dare you run away from your king?"},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian3","e":"stern","t":"I was born in your kingdom. But your service was hard, and your wages were death. So I looked for something better."},{"sc":"valley","w":"apollyon","e":"smirk","t":"Come back. I'll give you whatever our country has. Lots of people serve that Prince for a while, then come back to me. Do the same, and all will be well."},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian3","e":"stern","t":"I like His service, His wages, His servants, His government, His company and His country better than yours. I am His servant, and I will follow Him!","b":true},{"sc":"valley","w":"apollyon","e":"smirk","t":"But you've already failed Him! You fainted in the swamp. You took a wrong road. You slept and lost your roll. You nearly ran from the lions. And you love to show off about your journey!"},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian3","e":"smile","t":"All this is true, and much more. But the Prince whom I serve and honour is merciful, and ready to forgive.","b":true},{"sc":"battle","n":"Then Apollyon explodes with rage."},{"sc":"battle","w":"apollyon","e":"big","t":"I am the enemy of this Prince! I hate Him, His laws and His people. I have come out on purpose to stop you!"}],"quote":{"text":"The Prince whom I serve and honour is merciful and ready to forgive.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Know who you serve","text":"Apollyon tried three tricks: a threat (\"you're mine\"), a deal (\"come back, all will be well\"), and shame (\"look at your failures\"). Christian answered every one. He knew whose side he was on, and he admitted his mistakes without letting them define him. Leaders settle their loyalty before the pressure comes."},"think":"When someone throws your past mistakes at you to bring you down, what could you say back?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Christian meet Apollyon?","o":["In the Valley of Humiliation","At the Wicket Gate","On Hill Difficulty","In the Slough of Despond"],"why":"Right after leaving Palace Beautiful, down in the Valley of Humiliation."},{"q":"Why did Christian decide NOT to run away?","o":["His armour didn't cover his back","He was too tired to run","He wanted to make friends","He was lost"],"why":"Running would expose his back. Facing the enemy was safer."},{"q":"What did Apollyon claim about Christian?","o":["That Christian was one of his subjects","That Christian was his brother","That Christian owed him money","That Christian was a spy"],"why":"He said the whole City of Destruction belonged to him."},{"q":"How did Christian answer the list of his past failures?","o":["\"All this is true, but the Prince I serve is merciful\"","\"That's a lie!\"","\"You're right, I'll come back\"","He said nothing"],"why":"He was honest about his mistakes, and confident in his Prince's mercy."},{"q":"Which of these was NOT one of Apollyon's tricks?","o":["Offering Christian a crown of gold","A threat","A deal","Shame about the past"],"why":"Threat, deal, shame. Watch out for all three."}]},"pp4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"battle","w":"apollyon","e":"big","t":"Prepare to die! I swear by my den, you will go no farther. Here I will finish you!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"Apollyon spreads himself across the whole width of the road, and throws a flaming dart straight at Christian's chest!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"But Christian holds up his shield and catches it. Then he draws his sword. It's time to fight!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"Apollyon throws darts as thick as hail. Christian is wounded in his head, his hand and his foot. He steps back... then fights on bravely."},{"sc":"battle","n":"The fight goes on for more than half a day. Christian gets weaker and weaker from his wounds."},{"sc":"battle","n":"Then Apollyon sees his chance. He grabs Christian and slams him to the ground. Christian's sword flies out of his hand!"},{"sc":"battle","w":"apollyon","e":"big","t":"I'm sure of you now!"},{"sc":"battle","n":"Apollyon presses down on him. Christian starts to lose hope. But just as Apollyon raises his arm for the final blow, Christian stretches out his hand, and grabs his sword!"},{"sc":"battle","w":"christian4","e":"stern","t":"Rejoice not against me, O mine enemy: when I fall I shall arise!","b":true},{"sc":"battle","n":"He gives Apollyon a deep wound! The monster stumbles back."},{"sc":"battle","w":"christian4","e":"big","t":"Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors through Him that loved us!","b":true},{"sc":"battle","w":"apollyon","e":"shock","t":"AAARGH!"},{"sc":"valley","n":"Apollyon spreads his dragon wings and flies away. For a long time, Christian doesn't see him again."},{"sc":"valley","w":"christian4","e":"smile","t":"I give thanks to Him who saved me from the mouth of the lion, and helped me against Apollyon!"},{"sc":"valley","n":"Then a hand appears, holding leaves from the tree of life. Christian puts them on his wounds, and he is healed at once! He eats some bread, has a drink, and walks on with his sword in his hand."}],"quote":{"text":"Rejoice not against me, O mine enemy: when I fall I shall arise.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"When you fall, rise","text":"Christian was wounded, knocked down and lost his sword. It looked finished. But he reached out one more time. Leaders aren't people who never fall. They're people who get up again. And notice: he didn't win alone. He won \"through Him that loved us\"."},"think":"Think of a time you were knocked down: a failed test, a lost match, a hard week. What helped you get back up?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Christian catch Apollyon's flaming dart with?","o":["His shield","His sword","His bare hand","His helmet"],"why":"The shield from Palace Beautiful saved him."},{"q":"How long did the fight last?","o":["More than half a day","Five minutes","One week","One hour"],"why":"It was long and exhausting. Real battles often are."},{"q":"What happened when Apollyon slammed Christian down?","o":["His sword flew out of his hand","He fell asleep","He ran away","He found a key"],"why":"He was down and disarmed, but not defeated."},{"q":"What did Christian shout as he grabbed his sword?","o":["\"When I fall I shall arise!\"","\"I give up!\"","\"Help me, Pliable!\"","\"Set down my name!\""],"why":"Micah 7:8. Falling isn't the end if you rise."},{"q":"What healed Christian's wounds?","o":["Leaves from the tree of life","A doctor","Water from a river","Sleep"],"why":"The King sent healing after the battle."}]},"pp4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"shadow","n":"At the end of this valley is another one: the {Valley of the Shadow of Death}. The road to the Celestial City goes right through the middle of it."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"At its edge, two men come running back towards Christian."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"runaway","e":"shock","t":"Go back! Go back! If you love your life, go back!"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"worried","t":"Why? What did you see?"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"runaway","e":"shock","t":"The valley is as dark as pitch! We saw goblins and dragons. We heard howling and screaming. It's terrible!"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"stern","t":"From what you're telling me, this is still my road to the Celestial City."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"So the men run off, and Christian goes on with his sword drawn."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"The path is very narrow. On the right is a deep {ditch}. On the left is a dangerous {quag}, a swamp with no bottom."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"It's so dark that when Christian lifts his foot, he doesn't know where to put it down. When he steps away from the ditch, he nearly slips into the swamp."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Halfway through, right beside the path, is the mouth of a burning pit. Flames, smoke, sparks and horrible noises pour out. His sword is useless here."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"So Christian puts his sword away, and picks up another weapon, called {All-Prayer}."},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"worried","t":"O Lord, I beseech Thee, deliver my soul!","b":true},{"sc":"shadow","n":"He walks on like this for miles. Then he hears what sounds like a crowd of {fiends} coming towards him. He stops."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Should he go back? Then he remembers how many dangers he has already beaten. Going back could be even worse. He decides to keep going."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"The fiends come closer and closer. When they're almost on top of him, he shouts with all his strength:"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"stern","t":"I will walk in the strength of the Lord God!","b":true},{"sc":"shadow","n":"And the fiends back away. They come no farther."}],"quote":{"text":"I will walk in the strength of the Lord God.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Change your weapon, remember your wins","text":"In the dark valley, the sword didn't work, so Christian switched to All-Prayer. When fear said \"go back\", he remembered the battles he had already won. Leaders know some battles are won on your knees, and they use yesterday's victories as fuel for today's courage."},"think":"What is one 'win' from your past you can remember the next time you feel like giving up?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the two men running back tell Christian to do?","o":["Go back","Hurry up","Bring a torch","Wait for them"],"why":"They had a bad report and turned back. Christian kept going."},{"q":"What was on each side of the narrow path?","o":["A deep ditch on the right and a swamp on the left","Two lions","Two walls","A river and a mountain"],"why":"One wrong step either way was dangerous."},{"q":"Why did Christian put his sword away?","o":["It was useless against the fire and noise of the pit","It was broken","He was tired of carrying it","He lost it"],"why":"Some battles need a different weapon."},{"q":"What weapon did he use instead?","o":["All-Prayer","A bow and arrow","A torch","A big stick"],"why":"\"O Lord, I beseech Thee, deliver my soul!\""},{"q":"What made the fiends back away?","o":["Christian shouting, \"I will walk in the strength of the Lord God!\"","Christian running away","The sun rising","Christian's sword"],"why":"He didn't rely on his own strength."}]},"pp4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"shadow","n":"Then something strange happens. As Christian passes the burning pit, one of the wicked ones creeps up quietly behind him."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"It whispers terrible words into his ear, horrible things about the Prince he loves. And Christian thinks the words are coming from his own mind!"},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"worried","t":"How can I be thinking such things? What is wrong with me?"},{"sc":"shadow","n":"This troubles him more than anything so far. He doesn't know that he can stop his ears, or that those words are not really his."},{"sc":"shadow","n":"Then, in the darkness, he hears a man's voice somewhere ahead: \"Though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil; for Thou art with me.\""},{"sc":"shadow","w":"christian3","e":"big","t":"Someone else who loves God is in this valley! And if God is with him here, He's with me too, even if I can't feel it. Maybe I'll have company soon!"},{"sc":"dawn","n":"He calls out, but the man ahead doesn't answer. He thinks he's alone too. And then, slowly... the day breaks."},{"sc":"dawn","w":"christian3","e":"big","t":"He hath turned the shadow of death into the morning!","b":true},{"sc":"dawn","n":"Christian looks back. In the light, he sees the ditch, the swamp, the narrow path, and the goblins and dragons. They're far away now."},{"sc":"dawn","n":"The rest of the valley is even MORE dangerous, full of traps, nets, pits and holes. In the dark, he would never make it. But the sun is rising!"},{"sc":"dawn","w":"christian3","e":"smile","t":"His candle shineth on my head, and by His light I go through darkness.","b":true},{"sc":"cave","n":"At the end of the valley are old bones and ashes. Two giants once lived in a cave here, and hurt many pilgrims."},{"sc":"cave","n":"But one giant has been dead for years. The other is now so old and stiff that he can only sit in the mouth of his cave, grumbling at pilgrims as they pass."},{"sc":"road","n":"So Christian walks past safely, singing. Then he climbs a little hill... and sees someone walking on the road ahead of him! Who could it be? Find out in Chapter 5."}],"quote":{"text":"He hath turned the shadow of death into the morning.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Guard your mind, wait for morning","text":"Not every thought in your head is yours, or true. Some are lies whispered to bring you down. Christian didn't know that yet, but now you do. Reject the lie, and tell someone you trust. And remember: he wasn't alone in the valley, and morning came."},"think":"When scary or hurtful thoughts come, who are two people you could talk to?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did the terrible whispered words really come from?","o":["A wicked one who crept up behind him","Christian's best friend","The man ahead","A bird"],"why":"Christian thought they were his own thoughts. They weren't."},{"q":"What did Christian hear a voice ahead of him saying?","o":["\"Though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil\"","\"Go back!\"","\"Set down my name\"","\"I see no danger\""],"why":"Psalm 23:4. It told him he wasn't alone."},{"q":"What did Christian say when the day broke?","o":["\"He hath turned the shadow of death into the morning!\"","\"I'm tired\"","\"Where am I?\"","\"Let's go home\""],"why":"Dark seasons end."},{"q":"Why was it good that the sun rose when it did?","o":["The rest of the valley was full of traps and pits","He was cold","He wanted to sleep","He was hungry"],"why":"The light came just when he needed it most."},{"q":"What was the second old giant doing?","o":["Sitting in his cave, too old and stiff to chase anyone","Chasing Christian","Sleeping on the road","Guarding a gate"],"why":"Some old threats have lost their power."}]}}},"pp5":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who helped Christian up after he tripped?","o":["Faithful","Hopeful","Talkative","Evangelist"],"why":"Pride tripped him. A faithful friend lifted him."},{"q":"\"A saint abroad, and a devil at home\" described...","o":["Talkative","Faithful","Hopeful","Demas"],"why":"His words and his life didn't match."},{"q":"What did Faithful say he would buy at Vanity Fair?","o":["The truth","Gold","Fame","Nothing"],"why":"\"We buy the truth.\""},{"q":"How did Faithful reach the Celestial City?","o":["A chariot carried him up through the clouds","He walked","He swam the river","He took a boat"],"why":"Faithful to the end, he went straight home."},{"q":"Why did Hopeful become a pilgrim?","o":["He watched how Christian and Faithful lived","He found a map","Demas told him to","He was bored"],"why":"Example is powerful leadership."},{"q":"What was at the hill called Lucre?","o":["A silver mine","A palace","A lion","A river"],"why":"Demas's silver mine, a deadly trap."},{"q":"What opened the locks of Doubting Castle?","o":["A key called Promise","A sword","A big stone","Giant Despair's wife"],"why":"God's promises open the doors that despair locks."},{"q":"Why were the pilgrims caught in the Flatterer's net?","o":["They didn't read the shepherds' note","They were asleep","They were running","They were hungry"],"why":"Wise counsel only helps if you use it."},{"q":"How did they get through the Enchanted Ground?","o":["By keeping each other awake with good conversation","By running","By sleeping in turns","By riding a horse"],"why":"Friends who keep you awake are precious."},{"q":"Complete: \"I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the ___.\"","o":["faith","money","secret","crown"],"why":"2 Timothy 4:7. Finish well!"}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Who begins a journey of her own in Part II?","o":["Christiana, Christian's wife","Pliable","Giant Despair","Mrs Worldly Wiseman"],"why":"Christiana and her four sons set out next. See you in Part II!"},"choices":[{"title":"The viral challenge","q":"Everyone in your class is doing a viral video challenge that mocks one of your teachers. They want you to film it too, so it can go on TikTok.","o":[{"t":"Refuse kindly, and don't film or share it.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christian and Faithful in Vanity Fair, you don't have to buy what everyone is selling."},{"t":"Film it, but don't post it yourself.","f":"You're still helping the crowd. Faithful wouldn't buy even a little bit."},{"t":"Join in. It's only a joke.","f":"Mocking people isn't a joke to the person being mocked."},{"t":"Say nothing and laugh along.","f":"Silence in Vanity Fair is still a choice. Stand out, kindly."}]},{"title":"The silver mine","q":"A young man offers you ₦20,000 a week to help him send messages to strangers online after school. \"Easy money! Nobody gets hurt.\" You know it's a scam.","o":[{"t":"Refuse, and tell a parent or trusted adult.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! That's Demas's silver mine. People who go in don't come back the same."},{"t":"Do it just once to buy a phone.","f":"\"Just once\" is how By-ends ended up in the mine."},{"t":"Take the money but don't do the work.","f":"Still a trap. Stay on the road."}]},{"title":"Leading people the wrong way","q":"You lead your group project. You talked everyone into copying another group's work, and now the teacher has found out. The whole group is in trouble.","o":[{"t":"Tell the teacher it was your idea, apologise to your group, and redo the work properly.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Christian in the storm: \"I'm sorry, I led you here.\" Then lead them back."},{"t":"Say it was the group's idea.","f":"Christian didn't blame Hopeful. Leaders own their wrong turns."},{"t":"Deny everything.","f":"That locks you deeper in Doubting Castle."},{"t":"Quit the group.","f":"Leaders don't abandon the people they led into trouble. They lead them out."}]},{"title":"Deep water","q":"Your friend's father passed away a few weeks ago. She has stopped coming to youth fellowship and hardly talks to anyone.","o":[{"t":"Keep checking on her, sit with her, and remind her she isn't alone.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Be her Hopeful: \"Be of good cheer, I feel the bottom, and it is good.\""},{"t":"Leave her alone until she's better.","f":"In the deep river, Hopeful didn't swim ahead. He held his friend up."},{"t":"Tell her to get over it.","f":"Grief takes time. Kind words help more than hard ones."},{"t":"Talk about her behind her back.","f":"That's Vanity Fair behaviour. Be a friend instead."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"celestial","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 5 in real life."},{"sc":"road","n":"🤝 Pick friends who help you up, and be that friend. Faithful lifted Christian; Hopeful held his head above water."},{"sc":"fair","n":"⚖️ Buy the truth, and don't sell it. You don't have to follow every trend in Vanity Fair."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"🗝️ Use your keys. When you feel hopeless, God's promises open doors. And always talk to someone you trust."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"🐑 Read the note. Wise counsel only helps when you actually follow it."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"🏁 Finish well. Every journey has hard parts. Keep going, and help others finish too."}],"stops":{"pp5s1":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"From the little hill, Christian sees a man ahead of him. It's {Faithful}, his neighbour from the City of Destruction!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"Faithful! Stop! Wait for me, I'll walk with you!"},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"smile","t":"No, I can't stop. I'm running for my life!"},{"sc":"road","n":"So Christian runs as hard as he can. He catches up with Faithful... and runs PAST him. He smiles proudly. He's ahead now!"},{"sc":"road","n":"But he isn't watching his feet. He trips, falls flat, and can't get up, until Faithful comes and helps him."},{"sc":"road","n":"After that, they walk on together like brothers, sharing everything that has happened on their journeys."},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"worried","t":"I met a woman called Wanton. She flattered me and tried hard to lead me off the road. I shut my eyes and walked away."},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"worried","t":"Then an old man called Adam the First offered me a job with all the pleasures of the world. I nearly went! But I saw he would only make me his slave."},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"worried","t":"And a man called Shame kept mocking me: \"Only weak people follow God. Clever, rich people don't.\""},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"smile","t":"But I told myself: Shame tells me what people think. It tells me nothing about what God thinks."},{"sc":"road","n":"Soon they meet a tall man walking beside them. His name is {Talkative}. He can talk about ANYTHING: heaven, earth, the Bible, miracles..."},{"sc":"road","w":"talkative","e":"big","t":"I love to talk about good things! Whatever you want to discuss, I'm your man!"},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"I know him. He's from our town. He talks beautifully, but at home he lives badly. He is a saint abroad, and a devil at home.","b":true},{"sc":"road","w":"faithful","e":"stern","t":"Talkative, let me ask you one thing. Do you actually LIVE what you talk about?"},{"sc":"road","w":"talkative","e":"frown","t":"You're too personal. I don't want to talk with you any more. Goodbye!"},{"sc":"road","n":"And off he goes. Christian and Faithful walk on together."}],"quote":{"text":"He is a saint abroad, and a devil at home.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Stay humble, walk your talk","text":"The moment Christian got proud of overtaking his friend, he fell, and it was that same friend who helped him up. Talkative could talk beautifully, but his life at home didn't match. Leaders stay humble, choose friends who lift them, and live what they say."},"think":"Is there anything you talk about doing, but don't actually do? What would it take to start?","quiz":[{"q":"What happened when Christian ran past Faithful and smiled proudly?","o":["He tripped, fell and needed Faithful's help","He won a prize","He got lost","He met Evangelist"],"why":"Pride comes before a fall, and good friends help you up anyway."},{"q":"What did Shame say to Faithful?","o":["Only weak people follow God","Go back home","You're very brave","Let's be friends"],"why":"Shame mocks. Faithful answered that God's opinion matters more."},{"q":"What was Talkative good at?","o":["Talking about everything","Fighting giants","Running fast","Building houses"],"why":"He could talk about anything, but he didn't live it."},{"q":"\"A saint abroad, and a devil at home\" means...","o":["Good in public, bad in private","He travels a lot","He has two houses","He is very kind at home"],"why":"Real leaders are the same person in public and at home."},{"q":"What question made Talkative leave?","o":["\"Do you actually live what you talk about?\"","\"What's your name?\"","\"Where are you going?\"","\"Are you hungry?\""],"why":"The question about living it was too much for him."}]},"pp5s2":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Evangelist meets them again on the road. He smiles, encourages them, and warns them: \"In the next town, one of you may have to give his life for the truth. Be faithful to the end.\""},{"sc":"fair","n":"Soon they reach the town of Vanity. All year round, it holds a huge market called {Vanity Fair}."},{"sc":"fair","n":"EVERYTHING is for sale: houses, land, jobs, fame, titles, pleasures, gold and silver. There are cheats, fools and tricksters on every corner."},{"sc":"fair","n":"The road to the Celestial City goes right through the middle of it. Long ago, the Prince Himself walked through this fair, and bought nothing."},{"sc":"fair","n":"When Christian and Faithful walk in, everybody stares. Their clothes are different. The way they talk is different. And they don't look at any of the goods."},{"sc":"fair","n":"\"What will you buy? What will you buy?\" the traders shout at them."},{"sc":"fair","w":"faithful","e":"smile","t":"We buy the truth.","b":true},{"sc":"fair","n":"That makes the crowd angry. They mock the pilgrims, beat them, cover them in dirt, and lock them in a cage in the middle of the fair for everyone to laugh at."},{"sc":"fair","n":"But Christian and Faithful stay patient and kind. Some people in the fair start to think, \"Maybe these men are right.\""},{"sc":"court","n":"So they are put on trial. The judge is {Lord Hate-good}. The witnesses are Envy, Superstition and Pickthank. Every person on the jury hates them already."},{"sc":"court","w":"hategood","e":"frown","t":"You have disturbed our trade and insulted our ways. What do you say?"},{"sc":"court","w":"faithful","e":"stern","t":"I only spoke against what is against the Lord of heaven. I am ready to say it again."},{"sc":"court","n":"The jury decides: guilty. Faithful is sentenced to death, and the people of Vanity put him to death that same day."},{"sc":"sky","n":"But the storyteller sees a chariot and horses waiting behind the crowd. They carry Faithful up through the clouds, with trumpets sounding, the quickest way to the gate of the Celestial City."},{"sc":"road","n":"Christian is sent back to prison. But after a while, the One who rules over everything makes a way, and Christian escapes and goes on his journey."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"smile","t":"Well, Faithful, you have faithfully stood for your Lord. Your name will live on."}],"quote":{"text":"We buy the truth.","who":"Faithful"},"lesson":{"title":"Stand out, stay true","text":"In Vanity Fair, everything had a price and everyone followed the crowd. Christian and Faithful looked different, talked differently and wouldn't buy what everyone was selling. They stayed kind even when they were treated badly. Leaders don't sell the truth to fit in."},"think":"What does your 'Vanity Fair' look like: social media, music, fashion, school trends? What is the 'truth' you won't sell?","quiz":[{"q":"What was sold at Vanity Fair?","o":["Everything: houses, fame, pleasures, gold and more","Only fruit","Only books","Nothing"],"why":"Everything was for sale, but none of it lasted."},{"q":"What did Faithful say when the traders asked what they would buy?","o":["\"We buy the truth\"","\"We buy gold\"","\"Nothing, thank you\"","\"We buy food\""],"why":"Proverbs 23:23 says, \"Buy the truth, and sell it not.\""},{"q":"Why did the crowd stare at the pilgrims?","o":["Their clothes, speech and interests were different","They were very tall","They were singing","They were rich"],"why":"Pilgrims stand out in Vanity Fair."},{"q":"Who was the judge at the trial?","o":["Lord Hate-good","Evangelist","Goodwill","Mr Legality"],"why":"The trial was never going to be fair."},{"q":"What happened to Faithful after he died?","o":["A chariot carried him up to the Celestial City","He was forgotten","He went back home","He became a trader"],"why":"He was faithful to the end, and he went straight home to the King."}]},"pp5s3":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Christian doesn't walk alone for long. A young man from Vanity Fair runs to join him. His name is {Hopeful}."},{"sc":"road","w":"hopeful","e":"big","t":"I watched how you and Faithful lived and suffered in the fair. It made me want to follow the King too. Can I come with you?"},{"sc":"road","w":"hopeful","e":"smile","t":"And I'm not the only one. Others from the fair are thinking of following, too."},{"sc":"road","n":"Soon they meet a smooth, well-dressed man called Mr {By-ends}, from the town of Fair-speech."},{"sc":"road","w":"byends","e":"smirk","t":"I like religion when it walks in silver slippers, when the sun is shining and people clap for it. When it's in rags and trouble, I keep my distance."},{"sc":"road","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"If you come with us, you must follow the King in rain and in sunshine, in rags as well as in silver slippers."},{"sc":"road","w":"byends","e":"frown","t":"Then I'll find better company."},{"sc":"silver","n":"They cross a plain called Ease, and come to a little hill called {Lucre}. In its side is a silver mine. A man stands by the road, waving."},{"sc":"silver","w":"demas","e":"big","t":"Ho! Turn aside hither, and I will show you a thing! There's silver here. Dig a little and you'll be rich!","b":true},{"sc":"silver","w":"hopeful","e":"big","t":"Let's go and see!"},{"sc":"silver","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"Not I. I've heard about this place. Many people have died there. That treasure is a trap."},{"sc":"silver","n":"So they stay on the road. But Mr By-ends and his friends come along after them. At the first call from {Demas}, they go straight over to the mine..."},{"sc":"silver","n":"...and nobody ever sees them again."},{"sc":"silver","n":"A little further on, Christian and Hopeful find a strange pillar of salt shaped like a woman. Words are carved on it: \"Remember {Lot's wife}.\""},{"sc":"silver","w":"hopeful","e":"worried","t":"She looked back at what she loved more than God. I nearly did the same thing at the silver mine. I'm glad you stopped me."},{"sc":"river","n":"Then they come to a beautiful river with green trees and meadows full of flowers. They drink the water, eat the fruit, and rest safely for several days."}],"quote":{"text":"Ho! turn aside hither, and I will show you a thing.","who":"Demas"},"lesson":{"title":"Lead by example, and stay out of the mine","text":"Hopeful joined the journey because he watched how Christian and Faithful lived. Your example leads people, even when you don't know they're watching. And Demas shows how money can pull people off the road. Leaders aren't for sale."},"think":"Who might be watching the way you live right now? What are they learning from you?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Hopeful join Christian?","o":["He watched how Christian and Faithful lived","Christian paid him","He was lost","Evangelist sent him"],"why":"Their example led him, even in a hard place."},{"q":"Mr By-ends liked religion only when...","o":["It walked in silver slippers and people praised it","It rained","He was in trouble","He was alone"],"why":"He followed God only when it was popular and comfortable."},{"q":"What did Demas offer the pilgrims?","o":["Silver from a mine","A free meal","A shortcut","A horse"],"why":"Easy money, and a deadly trap."},{"q":"What happened to Mr By-ends and his friends?","o":["They went to the mine and were never seen again","They became pilgrims","They got rich","They went home"],"why":"The love of money swallowed them up."},{"q":"What was carved on the pillar of salt?","o":["\"Remember Lot's wife\"","\"Silver here\"","\"Turn back\"","\"Rest here\""],"why":"A warning not to look back at what pulls you away from God."}]},"pp5s4":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"After a while, the road gets rough and stony. Their feet start to hurt."},{"sc":"meadow","n":"Then they see a soft, green field just over a fence, running right beside the road. It's called {By-path Meadow}."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"Look, the path in that meadow goes the same way as our road, and it's much easier! Come, Hopeful, let's go over."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"hopeful","e":"worried","t":"But what if it leads us out of the way?"},{"sc":"meadow","w":"christian2","e":"smile","t":"It won't. Trust me."},{"sc":"meadow","n":"They follow a man called {Vain-confidence}, who says he knows the way. But night falls, he walks into a deep pit, and is never seen again."},{"sc":"storm","n":"Then a storm comes. Thunder, lightning, heavy rain. The water rises. They try to go back, but they can't find the way."},{"sc":"storm","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"Hopeful, I'm so sorry. I led you here. This is my fault."},{"sc":"storm","w":"hopeful","e":"smile","t":"Don't be too hard on yourself, brother. I forgive you. And I believe this will work out for our good."},{"sc":"castle","n":"Worn out, they fall asleep in a field. But the field belongs to {Giant Despair}, the owner of {Doubting Castle}."},{"sc":"castle","w":"despair","e":"frown","t":"Trespassers! Get up! You're coming with me!"},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"He drags them into a dark, smelly dungeon, from Wednesday morning until Saturday night, with no food, no water and no light."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"His wife, {Diffidence}, tells him to beat them, so he does. Then he tells them their situation is hopeless, and that they will never get out."},{"sc":"dungeon","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"Hopeful, what shall we do? I feel there's no way out."},{"sc":"dungeon","w":"hopeful","e":"smile","t":"Brother, remember how brave you were against Apollyon? And in the Valley of the Shadow of Death? Let's be patient a little longer."},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"On Saturday, around midnight, they start to pray. They keep praying until almost morning."},{"sc":"dungeon","w":"christian2","e":"shock","t":"What a fool am I, to lie in this dungeon when I could walk free! I have a key in my coat called {Promise}. I'm sure it will open any lock in Doubting Castle!","b":true},{"sc":"dungeon","n":"He tries the key in the dungeon door, and the lock clicks open! Then the outer door. Then the big iron gate. That lock is very stiff... but at last, it opens!"},{"sc":"castle","n":"The gate creaks loudly and wakes Giant Despair. He runs after them, but in the sunshine he falls into one of his fits and can't chase them."},{"sc":"road","n":"Back on the King's highway, they build a sign at the fence: \"This way leads to Doubting Castle. Giant Despair lives there. He wants to destroy pilgrims.\" Many who come later read it and are saved."}],"quote":{"text":"I have a key in my bosom called Promise, that will, I am persuaded, open any lock in Doubting Castle.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Own your wrong turn, and use your keys","text":"This time Christian led his friend the wrong way. He didn't make excuses: \"I'm sorry, this is my fault.\" Despair locked them up, but they had the key all along: God's promises. And afterwards they put up a sign to protect others. Leaders own their mistakes, hold on to God's promises, and warn the people coming behind them."},"think":"Feeling hopeless is like being locked in Doubting Castle. If you ever feel that way, who could you talk to? And which of God's promises could be your key?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Christian and Hopeful go into By-path Meadow?","o":["The road was rough and the meadow looked easier","Evangelist sent them","A lion chased them","They wanted to sleep"],"why":"Another easy shortcut, and another trap."},{"q":"Who led Hopeful into By-path Meadow?","o":["Christian","Faithful","Demas","Evangelist"],"why":"Even good leaders can lead people the wrong way. What matters is what they do next."},{"q":"What did Christian say when he realised his mistake?","o":["\"I'm so sorry, I led you here. This is my fault\"","\"It's your fault, Hopeful\"","\"It's the storm's fault\"","Nothing"],"why":"He owned it, and Hopeful forgave him."},{"q":"What was the name of the key that opened Doubting Castle?","o":["Promise","Hope","Faith","Freedom"],"why":"God's promises open the locks of despair."},{"q":"What did they do after they escaped?","o":["Put up a sign to warn other pilgrims","Went back to fight the giant","Rested in the meadow","Went home"],"why":"Leaders protect the people coming after them."}]},"pp5s5":{"story":[{"sc":"mountains","n":"At last they reach the {Delectable Mountains}: gardens, orchards, vineyards and fountains. Shepherds are looking after their sheep."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"The four shepherds are called Knowledge, Experience, Watchful and Sincere. They welcome the pilgrims warmly."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"knowledge","e":"smile","t":"Welcome to Immanuel's Land! Stay with us. Rest, and let us show you some things that will help you."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"From the top of a hill called Error, they see people far below who fell because they believed things that weren't true."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"From Mount Caution, they see men wandering blind among the tombs. They had climbed over that same fence into By-path Meadow, and Giant Despair caught them."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"That could have been us."},{"sc":"mountains","n":"Then the shepherds give them a telescope. Through it, far away, they see something like the gate of the Celestial City! Their hands shake with excitement."},{"sc":"mountains","w":"knowledge","e":"stern","t":"Here is a note with directions for the way. Watch out for the Flatterer. And don't fall asleep on the {Enchanted Ground}."},{"sc":"road","n":"Further on, a young man named {Ignorance} joins them. He says he'll be fine because he's a good person. He never came through the gate. He doesn't want to listen, so he walks behind them."},{"sc":"road","n":"Then a man in a bright white robe walks up. He's very friendly. \"I'm going to the Celestial City too! Follow me!\""},{"sc":"road","w":"flatterer","e":"smile","t":"Follow me! I know the way!"},{"sc":"road","n":"They follow him... and step right into a net! They're caught. The man's white robe falls off. He was the {Flatterer}!"},{"sc":"road","n":"A Shining One comes and cuts them free. \"Didn't the shepherds give you a note with directions?\" They forgot to read it! He corrects them firmly, and sets them back on the right road."},{"sc":"road","w":"atheist","e":"smirk","t":"Ha ha! The Celestial City? There's no such place! I've been looking for twenty years!"},{"sc":"road","w":"hopeful","e":"stern","t":"We saw its gate from the Delectable Mountains. We walk by faith."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"Now they reach the {Enchanted Ground}. The air is heavy and sleepy. Hopeful's eyes start to close."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"hopeful","e":"sleep","t":"Let's lie down here and take one nap."},{"sc":"enchanted","w":"christian2","e":"stern","t":"By no means! If we sleep here, we may never wake up. Let us not sleep, as others do, but let us watch and be sober."},{"sc":"enchanted","n":"So they keep each other awake by talking about how God led them. Hopeful tells his whole story, and the time flies. They cross the Enchanted Ground safely."}],"quote":{"text":"Let us not sleep, as do others; but let us watch and be sober.","who":"Christian"},"lesson":{"title":"Listen to wise counsel, and read the note","text":"The shepherds gave wise counsel and a note of directions. The pilgrims forgot to read it, and walked straight into the Flatterer's net. Advice only helps if you use it! And on the Enchanted Ground, they kept each other awake. Leaders seek wise counsel, follow it, and keep each other going."},"think":"Who are your 'shepherds', the wise people you can ask for advice? When did you last actually follow their advice?","quiz":[{"q":"What were the four shepherds called?","o":["Knowledge, Experience, Watchful and Sincere","Faith, Hope, Love and Joy","Simple, Sloth, Presumption and Pliable","Goodwill, Help, Evangelist and Faithful"],"why":"Wise shepherds with wise names."},{"q":"What did the pilgrims see through the shepherds' telescope?","o":["Something like the gate of the Celestial City","Giant Despair","Vanity Fair","The City of Destruction"],"why":"A glimpse of the goal kept them going."},{"q":"Why did the pilgrims get caught in the Flatterer's net?","o":["They forgot to read the shepherds' note","It was dark","They were asleep","Hopeful pushed them"],"why":"Good advice is useless if you don't use it."},{"q":"What did Atheist say?","o":["There is no Celestial City","Follow me","Buy the truth","I see no danger"],"why":"The pilgrims answered: we walk by faith."},{"q":"How did Christian and Hopeful stay awake on the Enchanted Ground?","o":["By talking about how God had led them","By drinking coffee","By running","By singing loudly"],"why":"Good conversation with a friend kept them alert."}]},"pp5s6":{"story":[{"sc":"beulah","n":"Now they enter the land of {Beulah}. The sun shines day and night. Birds sing. Flowers bloom everywhere. And they can see the Celestial City clearly!"},{"sc":"beulah","n":"The city is built of pearls and precious stones. Its streets are paved with gold. It shines so brightly that they have to look at it through a special glass."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"But between them and the city is a deep river. There is no bridge."},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Two Shining Ones meet them. \"You must go through the water. You'll find it deeper or shallower depending on how much you trust the King.\""},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"They step in. Almost at once, Christian starts to sink."},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"christian2","e":"worried","t":"I sink in deep waters; the billows go over my head!","b":true},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"hopeful","e":"big","t":"Be of good cheer, my brother, I feel the bottom, and it is good!","b":true},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"But Christian is overwhelmed by fear and darkness. He remembers all his old sins. Hopeful works hard to keep his friend's head above the water."},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"hopeful","e":"smile","t":"Brother, I see the gate, and people standing by it to welcome us! Be of good cheer. Jesus Christ makes you whole!"},{"sc":"deepriver","w":"christian2","e":"big","t":"Oh, I see Him again! And He tells me: \"When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee!\"","b":true},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"Suddenly, Christian finds ground under his feet. The rest of the river is shallow, and they walk out on the other side!"},{"sc":"celestial","n":"Shining Ones meet them and lead them up the hill to the city. Trumpeters come out playing music. Everyone is celebrating!"},{"sc":"celestial","n":"At the gate, they hand in their rolls, the same roll Christian once lost and found again. The King reads them and says, \"Open the gates!\""},{"sc":"celestial","n":"As they walk in, they are changed. Their clothes shine like gold. They're given crowns and harps. All the bells of the city ring for joy!"},{"sc":"celestial","n":"And they hear the words: \"Enter ye into the joy of your Lord.\""},{"sc":"celestial","n":"The storyteller watches through the open gate. \"When I had seen it,\" he says, \"I wished myself among them.\""},{"sc":"deepriver","n":"But the storyteller sees one more thing. Ignorance crosses the river easily in a ferry boat. At the gate he has no roll. He never came through the Wicket Gate. And he is taken away."},{"sc":"celestial","n":"Getting close is not the same as getting in. The way into the city is through the gate and the Cross, and the door is open to everyone who comes that way."},{"sc":"celestial","n":"THE END of Part I. But it's not the end of the story. Christian's wife Christiana and their four sons are about to begin a journey of their own..."}],"quote":{"text":"Be of good cheer, my brother, I feel the bottom, and it is good.","who":"Hopeful"},"lesson":{"title":"Finish well, and hold up your friend","text":"In the deepest water, Hopeful didn't swim ahead. He held his friend's head up and kept speaking hope. The journey that began with one scared man asking \"What shall I do?\" ended with two friends walking through the gate together. Leaders finish well, and they help others finish too."},"think":"Who in your life is in 'deep water' right now? How could you be their Hopeful this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What was between the pilgrims and the Celestial City?","o":["A deep river with no bridge","A tall wall","A giant","A desert"],"why":"Every pilgrim must cross the river."},{"q":"What did Hopeful say when Christian was sinking?","o":["\"Be of good cheer, my brother, I feel the bottom, and it is good\"","\"Swim faster!\"","\"Go back!\"","\"I'm sinking too\""],"why":"Hope spoken at the right time can hold someone up."},{"q":"What did Christian remember that helped him?","o":["\"When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee\"","The silver mine","Vanity Fair","Mr Worldly Wiseman's advice"],"why":"God's promise (Isaiah 43:2) brought him through."},{"q":"What did the pilgrims hand in at the gate?","o":["Their rolls","Gold coins","Their swords","A letter from Evangelist"],"why":"The roll Christian received at the Cross was his pass into the city."},{"q":"What happened to Ignorance?","o":["He had no roll, and was taken away from the gate","He became king","He went back home","He built a bridge"],"why":"Getting close isn't the same as getting in. The way is through the gate and the Cross."}]}}}});
